  "narrative": "No discovery assessments are due and no voluntary validation requests remain. I am registering ten dataset-internal comparisons that target unresolved central-map refinements rather than broad post hoc subgroup mining. First, I refine the conditionally supported PTEN-loss association within the TP53-intact, MSI-nonhigh background by splitting on SMARCA4-loss status and testing SMARCA4-loss as an effect modifier. These PTEN claims use direction -1; a signed estimate above +0.15 means PTEN loss is associated with stronger composite dependency, or stronger in SMARCA4-loss than SMARCA4-intact cells. Second, I test CDKN2A loss in TP53-intact, MSI-nonhigh backgrounds split by SMARCA4-loss and test SMARCA4-loss modification, because CDKN2A remains near-threshold and context-specific. Third, I add Cas9 technical robustness checks: whether high Cas9 activity modifies SMARCA4-loss, TP53-loss, KEAP1-loss, and MSI-high associations. The Cas9 eligibility uses a distinct Cas9 percentage variable, while the subgroup uses Cas9 score median split. Returned estimates and intervals are already signed to each registered hypothesis direction; positive signed values support the registered context or effect-modification direction. For interaction panels, near-zero results would support additivity or robustness, while clear threshold-level effects would indicate boundary conditions. All claims remain descriptive associations among measured cell-line characteristics in the supplied dataset, not causal, mechanistic, single-gene-essentiality, or externally generalizable claims. Multiplicity remains a concern, so only precise signed effects reasonably above the 0.15-unit threshold should be interpreted as meaningful modifications.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 13 explore plan, corrected. Mature accepted central map: SMARCA4 loss and MSI-high associated with stronger composite dependency; TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss associated with weaker composite dependency. PTEN loss is most reproducible in TP53-intact/MSI-nonhigh backgrounds but remains context dependent and uncertain globally or within SMARCA4-loss. CDKN2A remains near-threshold/unresolved. Validation budget is exhausted, so current work uses only supplied dataset analyses and avoids further random subgroup fishing.\n\nNew registered panel: (1-2) PTEN-loss in TP53-intact/MSI-nonhigh split by SMARCA4-loss status; (3) PTEN-loss modification by SMARCA4-loss within TP53-intact/MSI-nonhigh. (4-5) CDKN2A-loss in TP53-intact/MSI-nonhigh split by SMARCA4-loss status; (6) CDKN2A-loss modification by SMARCA4-loss within TP53-intact/MSI-nonhigh. (7-10) high Cas9 interaction panels for SMARCA4 loss direction -1, TP53 loss direction +1, KEAP1 loss direction +1, MSI-high direction -1, with eligibility using cas9_activity_pct and subgroup using cas9_activity_score median split to keep variables distinct.\n\nReturned estimates are already signed; positive values support the registered context/effect-modification direction against 0.15 units. I expect PTEN context contrasts to remain in stronger-dependency direction, CDKN2A/SMARCA4 context may identify only near-threshold effects, and Cas9 interactions mostly null if central effects are robust. Any interaction accepted only if clear and not opposite to pre-specified direction; otherwise treat as robustness/null rather than boundary condition."
